  "title": "AtomMem — code view",
  "subtitle": "What the MINE-USTC/AtomMem repo actually executes in the benchmarked LoCoMo pipeline. Lane = canonical stage (METHODOLOGY-SKELETON §2.2); empty lanes mean the stage does not exist here.",
  "source": "repo AtomMem @ 776f880   ·   verified against servers/atommem/verification.md (124 assertions: 101 ✓ / 2 ✗ / 20 ◐ / 1 ?)",
  "footer": "memory-bench · methodology flow · code view · every citation re-opened and confirmed during verification",
  "legend_notes": [
    "A6 is drawn paper_only: no weight files, no torch/transformers/peft in requirements.txt. A2's 'ext' node (the Fact Executor itself) is drawn paper_only too — the benchmarked pipeline reads pre-extracted facts straight off disk (evaluate_locomo.py:744), it never calls the extractor.",
    "B6's event_contexts is computed every query (_build_event_contexts, run_atommem_pipeline.py:399) and explicitly discarded three lines later (query_response.py:195/198/234) — a built-then-thrown-away step, not a missing one.",
    "A3 runs two independent similarity searches per fact: one for conflict detection (α/β=0.7/0.3, threshold 0.6, top-5) and an unrelated second one for event attribution (weights 0.7/0.3 from a different config pair, top-10) — neither reuses the other's candidates or scores.",
    "B5 SELECT exists here (GRAPH_MAX_SEED_FACTS=10) with no paper counterpart; the graph subsystem (B3/B4) is nominally optional via --disable-graph but runs by default in the benchmarked config."
  ],
